# The build context is the repo, so this is what keeps it from being a gigabyte.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
target
apps/web/build
apps/web/.svelte-kit
packages/crypto-wasm
bench
docs
*.log

# Secrets, and the near-misses.
#
# The build context is the whole repository and the Dockerfile does
# `COPY apps/server ./apps/server`, so a host key sitting in that directory —
# which is exactly where `pnpm host-key` writes one by default — was copied into
# the image. `docs/36` is blunt that neither key inside it can be regenerated,
# so an image pushed anywhere is every account on that Host.
#
# The patterns mirror `.gitignore` deliberately: the same file must not be
# committable *or* shippable, and two lists that disagree is how one of them
# gets forgotten.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
revel-host.json
**/revel-host.json
*host-key*.json
**/*host-key*.json
*.pem
**/*.pem
